<title>LEBANON: Lebanon's 1996 debt reaches $10.348 bln.</title>
<headline>Lebanon's 1996 debt reaches $10.348 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's finance ministry issued the following public debt figures to end of December 1996 (in millions of dollars unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>	    Net Domestic    Net Domestic   Foreign debt   Total</p>
<p>	   Debt (LBP blns)	Debt  Jan	   9,614		6,041	   1,305	  7,346</p>
<p> Feb	  10,032		6,317	   1,334	  7,651</p>
<p> Mar	  10,238		6,465	   1,363	  7,828</p>
<p> Apr	  10,668		6,752	   1,394	  8,146</p>
<p> May	  10,939		6,945	   1,526	  8,471</p>
<p> Jun	  11,236		7,152	   1,579	  8,731</p>
<p> Jul	  11,676		7,454	   1,574	  9,028</p>
<p> Aug	  11,961		7,657	   1,605	  9,262</p>
<p> Sep	  12,434		7,978	   1,666	  9,644</p>
<p> Oct	  12,733		8,183	   1,659	  9,842</p>
<p> Nov	  12,957		8,338	   1,702	 10,040</p>
<p> Dec	  13,315		8,579	   1,769	 10,348</p>
<p>($1 = 1,552 Lebanese pounds at end of December)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 345723 345740 745308 745309</p>
</text>
